}^{2},$ $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Find a repeated integral expression for the surface area of this surface." 13194139535508 true] [17592186352707 1113 #uuid "c26fb9d1-bd64-5afc-83db-47655a4115bf" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352707 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=x{y}^{2},\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/1419b067fe92945249655c5d29498aa4d3b0269d79ebd237fd9ed2a713b70b6a.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2})={y}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2})=2xy,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{({y}^{2})}^{2}+(2xy)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{y}^{4}+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+{y}^{4}+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352709 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352710 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352711 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352712 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352713 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352711 13194139535508 true] [17592186352708 1110 #uuid "6912ebe3-cece-58f0-b0