145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=x+{y}^{3},\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/87845c65dba220978ca81bd5a2b27816ca15f951cd14d8fe499ab43d3c64ef77.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{3})=1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+{y}^{3})=3{y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(1)^{2}+{(3{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{2+9{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{2+9{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352716 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352717 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352718 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352719 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352720 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352717 13194139535508 true] [17592186352715 1110 #uuid "ab020e3b-88b3-588c-8153-bdca8dced324" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352716 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{2+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352716 1111 #uuid "13fc3982-032f-58af-a621-8d4678e4bfa0" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352717 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{2+9{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352717 1111 #uuid "c4099523-985a-5c47-abb7-2ccdc44b9b2c" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352718 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{1+3{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352718 1111 #uuid "5384f711-be91-577f-8e2d-2d1518a1174b" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352719 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}2+3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352719 1111 #uuid "7d09cd96-af77-5852-9799-99e6e07e28db" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352720 1034 "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{1+y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352720 1111 #uuid "cb1b6292-639c-5e76-b6a2-18a0d7e009eb" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352721 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352722 13194139535508 true] [17592186352721 1089 "q-161144" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352721 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535508 true] [17592186352721 1100 "Find the surface area of the portion of the surface $z=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}y$ whose projection onto the $xy$-plane is bounded by $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352721 1113 #uuid "5eba7642-1f97-5622-aff0-b1dcdb8c116f" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352721 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}y,\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/f6200343142274ee2f5b3934cbe014ee24edf8177f3a544c38dc070bb7df83ef.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}y)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}y)=2\\sqrt{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+9{cos}^{2}⁡x+8}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{9(1+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡x}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot y\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=1+{cos}^{2}⁡x,$ we get $\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ u & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{2}^{1}\\sqrt{u}(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2({2}^{3/2}-1) \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352722 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352723 1319413953