question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/3c6c556ec90138fa1f0b599c6afed9d093e5c1b10f7751a5fbe55f0add617e1d.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-x)=-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y-x)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(-1)^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+1+4}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{6}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{6}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot [\\theta ]_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi \\sqrt{6}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352744 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352745 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352746 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352747 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352748 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352747 13194139535508 true] [17592186352743 1110 #uuid "ecc5366a-5a8f-5614-9695-de591b0558ef" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352744 1034 