e hemisphere $z=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ that is subject to the constraints ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1$ and $y\\ge 0.$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352756 1113 #uuid "f453f508-62af-5b81-9c75-095a29efd0bf" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352756 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}},\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 0},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/e7cb4d16f39d1c1e38d65000471cbc5ca1831a0bbc2cfc61c4f03d087d6a5125.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-{r}^{2}}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2r}{\\sqrt{4-{r}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2r}{\\sqrt{4-{r}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2r}{\\sqrt{4-{r}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=4-{r}^{2},$ we get $\\text{d}u=-2r\\,\\text{d}r.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2r}{\\sqrt{4-{r}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}r & =-\\pi {\\int }_{4}^{3}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{3}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 2{({u}^{1/2})}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot ({4}^{1/2}-{3}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi (2-\\sqrt{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352758 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352759 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352760 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352761 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352762 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352761 13194139535508 true] [17592186352757 1110 #uuid "5f736d1b-5c23-5447-9377-8fcbdb5fb852" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352758 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}(1-\\sqrt{3})" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352758 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352758 1111 #uuid "781b59d5-e6a5-5d74-a468-6219ac8976bb" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352759 1034 "\\pi (1-\\sqrt{3})" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352759 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352759 1111 #uuid "2464751c-3502-5a02-baca-f0920b98cf1c" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352760 1034 "\\pi (2-\\sqrt{6})" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352760 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352760 1111 #uuid "6b0047d7-bfbb-562f-a33c-6ab213589ff9" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352761 1034 "2\\pi (2-\\sqrt{3})" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352761 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352761 1111 #uuid "db6e7ab3-dfc6-526b-a640-de5bc3bd0ddb" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352762 1034 "2\\pi (3-\\sqrt{2})" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352762 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352762 1111 #uuid "843ffc41-e510-531f-8ab4-c363fda5ae12" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352763 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352764 13194139535508 true] [17592186352763 1089 "q-161176" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352763 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535508 true] [17592186352763 1100 "Find the surface area of the part of the hyperbolic paraboloid $y=1-{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}$ that is subject to the constraint ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 2.$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352763 1113 #uuid "4518bd85-5387-56bc-adec-8e46082ebb8b" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352763 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $y=f(x,z)$ with $(x,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\ny=1-{x}^{2}+{z}^{2},\\,(x,z)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 2},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/ab855ef2b9b5363005c14ea37470ed9ecb5853380a301341d20e2cd6095a5d1f.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂y}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1-{x}^{2}+{z}^{2})=-2x, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(1-{x}^{2}+{z}^{2})=2z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(-2x)^{2}+(2z)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4({x}^{2}+{z}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4({x}^{2}+{z}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=1+4{r}^{2},$ we get $\\text{d}u=8r\\,\\text{d}r.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ u & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r & =2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\int }_{1}^{9}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{[{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}{[{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}(27-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352765 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352766 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352767 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352768 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352769 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352769 13194139535508 true] [17592186352764 1110 #uuid "77910a6c-921d-56cd-9c6d-209378b5691f" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352765 1034 "\\frac{13\\pi \\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352765 1111 #uuid "60b5e676-c051-58bb-9b51-77c1086edd00" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352766 1034 "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{13}}{3}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352766 1111 #uuid "8e6e1d42-939c-5d37-bd6d-36efc5e49cee" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352767 1034 "\\frac{27\\pi }{2}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352767 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352767 1111 #uuid "e2077ed0-b4d5-53c6-a7f7-c620ce5b8662" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352768 1034 "\\frac{13\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352768 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352768 1111 #uuid "05ba2cfd-c137-5e91-ba1d-5fc01a0615fb" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352769 1034 "\\frac{13\\pi }{3}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352769 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352769 1111 #uuid "659f0184-8b96-5de3-bc98-f72341a41712" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352770 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352771 13194139535508 true] [17592186352770 1089 "q-161184" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352770 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535508 true] [17592186352770 1100 "Find the surface area of the portion of the surface $z=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}$ whose projection onto the $xy$-plane is bounded by $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352770 1113 #uuid "e885bc24-125b-51f1-be0b-b6d230809b4c" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352770 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/b9504140a4827cd74b74e8c23f76e1305389f1bc93a87834a37d4b20222e56f0.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})=x, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(x)^{2}+(0)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}\\cdot y\\,{|}_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352772 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352773 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352774 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352775 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352776 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352774 13194139535508 true] [17592186352771 1110 #uuid "012814c0-611d-509b-98e8-1d5b205b4ec7" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352772 1034 "10" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352772 1111 #uuid "0f6ca437-2c92-5e8c-ac6a-348dbf636110" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352773 1034 "8" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352773 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352773 1111 #uuid "7b610b8c-1a13-5f6a-a40a-22f9dad26e1e" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352774 1034 "2" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352774 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352774 1111 #uuid "7070b859-eba5-56d6-81a1-5cb199364789" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352775 1034 "4" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352775 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352775 1111 #uuid "8079e995-762b-54f2-89cf-169ccd1b1f8c" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352776 1034 "5" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352776 1111 #uuid "9e5ee948-d716-50db-8704-3cb99fc6cb3f" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352777 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352778 13194139535508 true] [17592186352777 1089 "q-161213" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352777 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535508 true] [17592186352777 1100 "Find the surface area of the part of the surface $x={y}^{2}+\\sqrt{3}z$ whose projection onto the $yz$-plane is bounded by $z=y,$ $y=1,$ and the $y$-axis." 13194139535508 true] [17592186352777 1113 #uuid "9bc498fc-2992-50fe-8096-df2abc6f57f0" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352777 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $x=f(y,z)$ with $(y,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nx={y}^{2}+\\sqrt{3}z,\\,(y,z)\\in D,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le y},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/0cf571155f2a4cd78d83c4808326cd8102badb3c22f43e00d95aee2494859f48.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+\\sqrt{3}z)=2y, \\\\ \\frac{∂x}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}+\\sqrt{3}z)=\\sqrt{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(2y)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{4+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot z\\,{|}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot y\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=1+{y}^{2},$ we get $\\text{d}u=2y\\,\\text{d}y.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot y\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({2}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(2\\sqrt{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352779 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352780 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352781 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352782 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352783 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352781 13194139535508 true] [17592186352778 1110 #uuid "b6ee7bef-542a-5dcf-8a77-4fbe6d9b2eb9" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352779 1034 "\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{3}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352779 1111 #uuid "c02537e7-f23d-5ad0-997c-a276787fac17" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352780 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352780 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352780 1111 #uuid "b64b4336-74bf-5bf8-9125-6c9898a23f50" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352781 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}(2\\sqrt{2}-1)" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352781 1111 #uuid "ea0d2795-c1a3-528a-a63a-3ad8dc12d636" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352782 1034 "2\\sqrt{2}-3" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352782 1111 #uuid "55f360fa-a32f-52cd-b429-9ed2837a0d5a" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352783 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{3}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352783 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352783 1111 #uuid "6ec1dcab-0684-54f8-b4f2-6822ef83732d" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352784 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352785 13194139535508 true] [17592186352784 1089 "q-161214" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352784 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535508 true] [17592186352784 1100 "Find the surface area of the part of the surface $x={e}^{y}-z$ whose projection onto the $yz$-plane is bounded by $z={e}^{2y},$ $y=0,$ $y=\\frac{1}{2},$ and the $y$-axis." 13194139535508 true] [17592186352784 1113 #uuid "fb7c50d7-7f31-5b23-9d88-d62a8dd861b7" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352784 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $x=f(y,z)$ with $(y,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nx={e}^{y}-z,\\,(y,z)\\in D,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le z\\le {e}^{2y}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066535/assets/9cae5b68f77c2d79df8a81d0421146ac2bbe618c6065a457c33c86caceeb1327.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{y}-z)={e}^{y}, \\\\ \\frac{∂x}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{y}-z)=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+({e}^{y})^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{e}^{2y}+2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{2y}}\\sqrt{{e}^{2y}+2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2y}+2}\\cdot z\\,{|}_{z=0}^{z={e}^{2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2y}+2}\\cdot {e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u={e}^{2y}+2,$ we get $\\text{d}u=2{e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & 0 & 1/2 \\\\ u & 3 & e+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\sqrt{{e}^{2y}+2}\\cdot {e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{3}^{e+2}\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{3}^{e+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((e+2)^{3/2}-{3}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(e+2)^{3/2}-3\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352786 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352787 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352788 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352789 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352790 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352790 13194139535508 true] [17592186352785 1110 #uuid "f99c02c6-3008-57d5-8018-eba0452dce58" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352786 1034 "\\sqrt{e+2}-\\sqrt{3}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352786 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352786 1111 #uuid "eb91da2b-f51d-5774-a7e0-86d658da95c2" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352787 1034 "\\frac{3(e+2)^{3/2}+9\\sqrt{3}}{4}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352787 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352787 1111 #uuid "754a4631-3a1f-506d-ae66-8314a4a550e7" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352788 1034 "2-3\\sqrt{3}+e" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352788 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352788 1111 #uuid "b9b1b74e-eca4-5e1f-a7de-e68b9788858e" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352789 1034 "\\frac{2(e-1)^{3/2}}{3}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352789 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352789 1111 #uuid "43918ec9-5ef2-5cc2-9671-29203784473c" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352790 1034 "\\frac{(e+2)^{3/2}-3\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352790 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535508 true] [17592186352790 1111 #uuid "7356a9d9-e023-5204-8bcb-e8761f9d8c01" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352791 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352792 13194139535508 true] [17592186352791 1089 "q-161230" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352791 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535508 true] [17592186352791 1100 "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(y,z)\\,:\\,\\boxed{}\\,}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the part of the surface $x={y}^{3}+{e}^{z}$ that lies inside the elliptical cylinder $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}=1.$ From left to right, what are the missing expressions?" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352791 1113 #uuid "528b3e83-41c0-5efb-a577-4265eb93ac16" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352791 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $x=f(y,z)$ with $(y,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nx={y}^{3}+{e}^{z},\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\le 1.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}+{e}^{z})=3{y}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂x}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{3}+{e}^{z})={e}^{z},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(3{y}^{2})}^{2}+({e}^{z})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+9{y}^{4}+{e}^{2z}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$\\,$ $\\sqrt{1+9{y}^{4}+{e}^{2z}}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\le 1.$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352793 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352794 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352795 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352796 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352797 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352795 13194139535508 true] [17592186352792 1110 #uuid "7ed312c5-b769-5c42-9848-b1307a5424b5" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352793 1034 "$\\sqrt{1+9{y}^{2}+{e}^{2z}}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\ge 1$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352793 1111 #uuid "18d21f2c-913f-535f-b3b3-45f7aa932a77" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352794 1034 "$\\sqrt{2{y}^{4}+{e}^{z}}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}=1$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352794 1111 #uuid "a534416e-2ec3-53c7-8423-18959d781796" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352795 1034 "$\\sqrt{1+9{y}^{4}+{e}^{2z}}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\le 1$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352795 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352795 1111 #uuid "86c95757-b5d0-555b-89c7-7c8cbe99b053" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352796 1034 "$\\sqrt{2{y}^{2}+{e}^{z}}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\le 1$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352796 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352796 1111 #uuid "80375b1a-abae-52c4-9abf-19ec3ea08b61" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352797 1034 "$\\sqrt{{y}^{3}+{e}^{2z}-1}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\ge 1$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352797 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352797 1111 #uuid "caf75422-2788-58e4-93fe-aba0b12689f2" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352798 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352799 13194139535508 true] [17592186352798 1089 "q-161443" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352798 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535508 true] [17592186352798 1100 "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(x,z)\\,:\\,\\boxed{}\\,}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the part of the surface $y=\\frac{1}{xz}$ that lies inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=2.$ From left to right, what are the missing expressions?" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352798 1113 #uuid "49516f7e-9986-5620-a6d8-96d7b448f56b" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352798 1145 "For a surface $S$ defined by $y=f(x,z)$ with $(x,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{xz},\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂y}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{xz})=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}z}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{1}{xz})=-\\frac{1}{x{z}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}z})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{x{z}^{2}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}{z}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}{z}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}{{x}^{4}{z}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$\\,$ $\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}{{x}^{4}{z}^{4}}}\\,$ and ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 2.$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352800 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352801 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352802 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352803 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352804 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1041 "selection" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352801 13194139535508 true] [17592186352799 1110 #uuid "53d003f1-52c3-5c16-a553-1c7ce00fae13" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352800 1034 "$\\frac{1}{xz}\\,$ and ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=2$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352800 1111 #uuid "95a93f62-783d-5f91-9dda-70103da50dfb" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352801 1034 "$\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}{{x}^{4}{z}^{4}}}\\,$ and ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 2$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352801 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352801 1111 #uuid "1faf39be-e5cd-551e-88d7-25d3b3fbe22d" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352802 1034 "$\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x+z}{{x}^{4}{z}^{4}}}\\,$ and ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=2$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352802 1111 #uuid "188ab2a2-54ea-5579-9c49-50616578c24b" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352803 1034 "$\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x+z}{{x}^{2}{z}^{2}}}\\,$ and ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\ge 2$" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352803 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535508 true] [17592186352803 1111 #uuid "72d48091-8d39-5336-af4d-95a64de51b86" 13194139535508 true] [17592186352804 103